# Site guide email

`src/lib/site-guide.ts` is the source of truth for the optional welcome-email overview (user vs administrator).

When you add, rename, or remove something people can see or do in the UI:

1. Update the matching section in `src/lib/site-guide.ts` in the same change.
2. Users get catalog, search, filters, details, versions, Back/focus, lists, account settings (email, password, notifications, delete account), and new-movie emails.
3. Administrators get the user sections plus folders, scans, review, library edit/hide/art, users, SMTP, TMDB key, backup download/restore, and the Video files vs Movies overview.
4. Write the guide in English (app UI language), short bullets, no internal implementation details.
5. Do not mention passwords in the guide body; the welcome lines already say the admin set one.
